Yes you are.  A player using my (fairly traditional) approach - use
the fact that your nemesis is created asleep and meditating - has a
chance of getting the first attack; a player using your proposed approach
will have wasted that opportunity.  In addition, you've consumed resources
(teleportation magic, etc) that you could otherwise have used to save
your life (or save yourself some time) on a different occasion.

>So you might as well if you don't have a Wand of death 

If I'm facing one of the more dangerous quests, I'll do the castle
before I do the quest.  I frequently end up doing the castle first
*anyway*.  Once you've done the castle, if you want a wand of death, you
can have a wand of death.  The Samurai quest usually contains a few of
the damn things in the hands of Ashikaga's minions, so you need MR or
reflection *anyway*.

The class I'd most want to do the quest first with - Valkyrie - is the
class most able to do the quest the traditional way.

And... now that I think about it more deeply, your tactic will fail far
more often than it succeeds.

Action 1: Teleport artifact and nemesis.  This will awaken your nemesis
and break its meditation.  Your nemesis may then, I think, get an
opportunity to act; if it acts, it will teleport to where the quest
artifact is.  Sucks to be you.

Action 2: Use object detection magic if the artifact hasn't landed in
your line of sight with no other items or monsters in the square.  At
this point, your nemesis is quite likely to have taken an action, so
the quest artifact *will* be in their possession.  Again, it sucks to
be you in this situation.

Action 3: Teleport to artifact if your nemesis has somehow not acted,
with autopickup set to collect it.  If your nemesis hasn't acted by this
point, it will teleport next to you and makes a SAMU attack against you;
if it acted at any previous point.  You might or might not still have
the quest artifact after this.

Action 4: If you still have the artifact, quaff cursed potion of gain
level, leaving the level.  Unfortunately for you, your nemesis is an
M2_STALK monster, which means that if you leave a level *by any means*
while they are adjacent to you, *they will come with you*.

